\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Definition}
\title{Update proposal}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{optimization}

\p{Let #{z_n} denote optimizer state. An \strong{update proposal} is a map}

##{
  U(\theta_n,z_n;\rho,Z,\Gamma,m^{(n)})
  =(\widehat\theta_{n+1},\widehat z_{n+1},d_n),
}

\p{where #{d_n} is a diagnostic record computed before commitment. The inputs
include the selected rollout, feedback, credit targets, and attempt-local
masks. The output is a candidate parameter transition.}

\p{This is an FTIP synthesis. It combines policy optimization with a
pre-optimizer diagnostic. A proposal objective appears in
\citet{Section 3}{schulman2017proximal}.}

\p{The procedure in \citet{Section 3.3}{miao2026when} computes a head-gradient
diagnostic before Adam and may discard the proposed reuse update.}

\p{Proposal separates computation from state change. It therefore makes a
rejected gradient pass visible in the cost account.}
